<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Anglovaal pre-exepts H1 shr up 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Anglovaal pre-exepts H1 shr up 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-excepts (cts) 488	  vs 381</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	549	  vs 423</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  57	   vs 47</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    347.3	vs 267.6</p>
<p>    Operating profit	 625.3	vs 512.1</p>
<p>    Investment income	 12.8	vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains	 54.6	vs  49.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    692.7	vs 572.6</p>
<p>    Tax			  160.5	vs 161.7</p>
<p>    Equity-accted earnings  90.0	vs 107.5</p>
<p>Attrib to outside shareholders</p>
<p>     of subsidiaries	 274.9	vs 250.8</p>
<p>    Turnover		 8,739.1	vs 7,569.7</p>
<p>Div payable April 25</p>
<p>on register March 27</p>
<p>Full name: Anglovaal Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptional gains mainly reflect profits on disposals.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast EPS of 497.7 with a range 490.1-509.0 and a dividend of 62.2 with a range 61.1-63.5.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
